<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jind Kaur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1863</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Maharani Jind Kaur, Rani Jindan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jind Kaur was the youngest wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Maharaja Ranjit Singh</a> and mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duleep-singh">Duleep Singh</a>, the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. She acted as regent for her young son from 1843, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> the British removed her from power, imprisoned and exiled her. She escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> in 1849, was reunited with her son in 1861 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1863.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jind-kaur.jpg" alt="Jind Kaur" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Richmond · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharani_Jind_Kaur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
